# Local-only secrets. Never commit real values. Copy to .dev.vars and fill in.
# Production equivalents: `wrangler secret put GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` etc.

# OAuth 2.0 Client credentials from Google Cloud Console
# (APIs & Services → Credentials → Create OAuth client ID → Web application)
# Add the redirect URI: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Signs nothing today (Google verifies tokens), but reserved for future
# cookie-level integrity checks and CSRF tokens. Generate: `openssl rand -hex 32`
SESSION_SECRET=""